{"title":"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 4a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Formula_for_Sum)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Formula for Sum)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>geometric</i> sequence is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by multiplying it by a non-zero constant, called the <i>common ratio</i>. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455e64dfca6a85a26a7b425a8df331c412a8466b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 10, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> is a geometric sequence with three terms and a common ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the sum of the first three terms of a geometric sequence with a common ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and whose second term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We divide the second term by the common ratio to get the first term:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3ee621e27ac9cfbd93deb125d75cf43cf8ff5b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\div \\frac{3}{5} = 45 \\times \\frac{5}{3} = 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"175\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Next, we multiply the second term by the common ratio to get the third term:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/47390e15fca22b417d2011dd024f4ce3244d3350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\times \\frac{3}{5} = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the terms is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbfabf8243c1b0b2b43d6a5e3838fe872bb7244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75 + 45 + 27 = 120 + 27 = \\boxed{147}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"256\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Formula_for_Sum.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Formula_for_Sum)\">Solution 2 (Formula for Sum)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Formula for Sum)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use the same method as Solution 1 to find that the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we can then use the formula for the sum of a geometric sequence.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1ab35a236b70e5cd0f0c8485609bc67485ac1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = \\frac{a_1\\left( 1-r^{n} \\right)}{1 - r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"134\" height=\"42\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> represents the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the sequence, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the common ratio. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fee012b15c661c6a53db88d3d8e19c1ac9cff6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bede03ea14db4aa32a7d20d908662d37b46b6937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, so we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\tS_3 &amp;= \\frac{75\\left(1 - \\left( \\frac{3}{5} \\right)^{3}\\right)}{1 - \\frac{3}{5}} = \\frac{75 \\left(1 - \\frac{27}{125}\\right)}{\\frac{2}{5}}\\\\\n\t&amp;=\\left(75 \\times \\frac{98}{125}\\right) \\times \\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n\t&amp;=3 \\times 49\\\\\n\t&amp;=\\boxed{147}.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032329\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 77/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 404/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3235/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.675      1 2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    6.675      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36325:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018032329 and revision id 281370. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}